WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.181
Download models from an approved source and verify the intended revision before spending time loading them.

00:00:06.181 --> 00:00:09.982
A persistent cache or reusable disk can reduce repeated transfers,

00:00:09.982 --> 00:00:13.783
but it continues to generate cost and must be protected.

00:00:13.783 --> 00:00:14.923
For disposable instances,

00:00:14.923 --> 00:00:19.484
consider whether a clean automated download is safer and cheaper than retaining

00:00:19.484 --> 00:00:21.765
a large cache between infrequent sessions.

00:00:21.765 --> 00:00:27.466
Quantization reduces memory demand and may allow a model to run on a smaller rental.

00:00:27.466 --> 00:00:31.267
Evaluate the quality and speed tradeoff with the actual task.

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:35.828
Configure an inference server with explicit model, context, batch, and GPU settings,

00:00:35.828 --> 00:00:38.489
then expose it through an authenticated API.

00:00:38.489 --> 00:00:40.769
Keep the endpoint private while testing,

00:00:40.769 --> 00:00:44.190
and apply request limits and timeouts before sharing it.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:47.991
Concurrency controls simultaneous sequences and increases cache and compute pressure.

00:00:47.991 --> 00:00:52.172
Batching can improve total throughput but may delay an individual request.

00:00:52.172 --> 00:00:56.733
Measure time to first output, prompt-processing speed, generation speed, queue time, errors,

00:00:56.733 --> 00:00:58.633
and completed work per hour.

00:00:58.633 --> 00:01:02.054
Include network latency between the client and rental region.

00:01:02.054 --> 00:01:06.995
A fast benchmark inside the instance may not represent the user's end-to-end experience.

00:01:06.995 --> 00:01:10.796
Test real prompts, context lengths, documents, images, and failure cases.

00:01:10.796 --> 00:01:15.737
Watch VRAM, GPU utilization, CPU, RAM, disk, and network while the test runs.

00:01:15.737 --> 00:01:19.918
If the accelerator remains underused, identify whether tokenization, data transfer, queueing,

00:01:19.918 --> 00:01:24.099
or an unsupported backend is responsible before renting a larger device.

00:01:24.099 --> 00:01:28.280
The goal is the lowest-cost configuration that completes the workload reliably,

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:30.180
not the largest GPU available.
